config {
  type: "assertion",
  tags: ["meta", "monitoring"],
  description: "stg_meta_age_gender must carry every impression the raw age_gender table holds. This is the guard that was missing on 2026-11-09, when the staging key turned out to be one column short of the source's and had been silently dropping rows for five weeks."
}

-- An assertion FAILS if it returns rows. Empty result = healthy.
--
-- WHAT THIS REPLACED, AND WHY.
--
-- Until 2026-11-09 this assertion counted duplicates in
-- fct_meta_age_gender_daily on date + campaign + age + gender. That check
-- was already done by the uniqueKey assertion in the fact's own config, and
-- it could not fail: staging de-duplicated on exactly those four columns,
-- so the fact was unique by construction whatever the source did.
--
-- It was watching the one thing that could not go wrong, while the thing
-- that did go wrong went unwatched for five weeks.
--
-- THE SOURCE GRAIN WAS ONE COLUMN FINER THAN OURS. age_gender also splits
-- by ad_format_asset. Staging keyed without it, so the QUALIFY treated a
-- second asset id as a re-sync of the first and threw it away. Measured
-- on the raw table that day:
--   310,121 rows for 300,234 date+campaign+age+gender keys
--   9,496 keys with more than one row
--   all 9,496 differing on ad_format_asset, NONE on _weld_synced
-- Cost in October alone: 694,133 impressions, 3,929.75 spend.
--
-- Every assertion in the project passed throughout. Grain was unique,
-- nothing was null, freshness was current. Loss is invisible to all three.
--
-- SO THIS NOW RECONCILES VOLUME instead of checking shape. Staging must
-- carry what the source holds. It is the only check that would have caught
-- what happened, and the only one that catches it happening again -- in
-- either direction, since a QUALIFY that stops de-duplicating a source
-- that starts re-syncing shows up here as staging being LARGER.
--
-- THE SOURCE IS A HAND-BUILT WELD MODEL. It does not follow the
-- connector's demographics_* naming and it has already changed shape once,
-- from rolling 7-day windows to daily on 2026-10-12. A new breakdown
-- column appearing is not a hypothetical.
--
-- TOLERANCE IS ZERO. Staging applies no filter, so any difference at all
-- is a key that no longer matches the source's.

WITH sursa AS (
  SELECT
    DATE(date)              AS zi,
    SUM(CAST(impressions AS INT64)) AS impresii
  FROM ${ref({ schema: constants.DATASETS.meta, name: "age_gender" })}
  GROUP BY 1
),

staging AS (
  SELECT
    date                    AS zi,
    SUM(impressions)        AS impresii
  FROM ${ref("stg_meta_age_gender")}
  GROUP BY 1
)

SELECT
  s.zi,
  s.impresii                      AS impresii_in_sursa,
  IFNULL(g.impresii, 0)           AS impresii_in_staging,
  s.impresii - IFNULL(g.impresii, 0) AS diferenta,
  'stg_meta_age_gender does not match facebook_ads_weld.age_gender. A positive difference means staging is dropping rows -- check whether the source gained a breakdown column that is missing from the QUALIFY key. A negative one means it has stopped de-duplicating.' AS actiune
FROM sursa s
LEFT JOIN staging g USING (zi)
WHERE s.impresii <> IFNULL(g.impresii, 0)
